From: notrealOS <53965041+notrealdotmp4@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] software_isp: debayer_egl: Meter the whole visible frame

The stats window was only sized, never positioned, so AGC/AWB looked at
the top-left corner of the sensor for any output smaller than the input.
---
--- a/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp
@@ -355,10 +355,14 @@
 	}
 
 	/*
-	 * Don't pass x,y from window_ since process() already adjusts for it.
-	 * But crop the window to 2/3 of its width and height for speedup.
+	 * process() hands the whole input buffer to the stats, so the window
+	 * must be in input coordinates. Rectangle(window_.size()) metered only
+	 * the top-left corner of the sensor (e.g. 1920x1080 of 4080x3072),
+	 * which left scenes with a dark corner badly overexposed. Meter the
+	 * whole area the output shows instead.
 	 */
-	stats_->setWindow(quadBayer_ ? window_ : Rectangle(window_.size()));
+	stats_->setWindow(quadBayer_ ? window_
+				     : quadBayerStatsWindow(inputCfg.size, outputCfg.size));
 
 	inputBufferCount_ = inputCfg.bufferCount;
 	outputBufferCount_ = outputCfg.bufferCount;
